title: Rock Ballad in Six
key: D
tempo: 66
meter: 6/8
style: rock

// The rock ballad in six-eight: two slow beats to the bar, three eighths in
// each. The verse walks the bass down from the one through the five over its
// third to the six and the four; the chorus starts on the four and turns on
// the four and the five, a chord a beat, back into the verse; the bridge sits
// on the six minor, climbs to the four and the five, and lands on the five.
[Verse]
| D | A/C# | Bm | G |
| D | A/C# | G  | A |

[Chorus]
| G | A | D | Bm  |
| G | A | D | G A |

[Verse]

[Chorus]

[Bridge]
| Bm | F#m | G | D |
| Em | F#m | G | A |

[Chorus]
